https://github.com/PadeanuTudor/ADS-Implementations/tree/main/Live%20Leaderboard

How to use:


- Download the Live Leaderboard folder and open it in your Java IDE of choice
- Run it
- In the terminal, an self-explanatory menu should show.

- 1 to check top k players, the program will ask for a k then display the top k players
- 2 to add a new player, program will ask you for a player name and after that for a score
- 3 to remove a player, program will ask for a player name to remove
- 4 to update a player's score, program will ask for a bonus to be added to the player's score, either negative or positive
- 0 to close the program
- entering anything else will go back to the menu


Important:
- The leaderboard is empty by default, and it doesn't save it in-between runs
- The program doesn't strip whitespace from player's name, so "player" and "player    " aren't the same
